Local/on-prem
MySQL
  │
 PVC
  │
Local Persistent Volume
  │
Worker VM disk
AWS EKS
MySQL StatefulSet
       │
mysql-data-mysql-0
       │
      PVC
       │
 StorageClass gp2
       │
 EBS CSI Driver
       │
   AWS EC2 API
       │
 Amazon EBS Volume

Initially:

PVC → Pending ❌

After adding the EBS CSI integration:

card-transactions-pvc    Bound   1Gi
mysql-data-mysql-0       Bound   2Gi

That is a real cloud-migration change: the application abstraction (PVC) remains mostly the same while the underlying storage implementation changes from local disk to AWS EBS.

6. Helm environment strategy

We kept the normal chart:

helm/
└── payment-api/
    ├── Chart.yaml
    ├── values.yaml
    ├── values-eks.yaml
    └── templates/

values.yaml represents defaults/local configuration.

values-eks.yaml provides AWS-specific overrides such as EBS storage configuration.

Deployment:

helm upgrade --install card-processing . ^
  -n card-processing ^
  -f values-eks.yaml ^
  --wait

This gives us:

             SAME HELM CHART
                    │
          ┌─────────┴─────────┐
          ▼                   ▼
     values.yaml        values-eks.yaml
          │                   │
          ▼                   ▼
    Local Kubernetes        AWS EKS

That is much better than copying the entire Kubernetes application into an aws/ directory and maintaining two versions.

7. Problems we actually encountered

These are valuable interview material because they demonstrate troubleshooting rather than just a successful deployment.

Problem	Root cause	Fix
kubectl Unauthorized	AWS credential/profile issue	Correct AWS profile + kubeconfig
EKS API timeout	Cluster/API connectivity	Validated endpoint/network access
PVC Pending	EBS CSI provisioning unavailable	Added EBS CSI + IAM/OIDC
Helm timed out	MySQL/Audit waiting on PVC	Fixed storage provisioning
Payment Service had no endpoints	Service selector didn't match pod labels	Corrected Helm Service selector
/history returned 500	transactions table missing in carddb	Fixed DB init ConfigMap
Table existed in wrong DB	Init used auditdb, app used carddb	Standardized on carddb
/audit returned 500	Test JSON used transaction_id; app expected transaction	Corrected request
Persistence needed validation	Needed proof beyond PVC Bound	Stored record, restarted pod, queried again
